 "name": "arduino-lcd2004-i2c",
 "description": "LiquidCrystal_I2C's HelloWorld on an Uno with a 20x4 HD44780 LCD behind the common PCF8574 I2C backpack, wired as that board is: P0 to RS, P1 to R/W, P2 to E, P4..P7 to D4..D7, P3 switching the backlight through 4.7 kOhm and an NPN transistor in the cathode, A0..A2 pulled up by 10 kOhm (address 0x27), 4.7 kOhm pull-ups on SDA and SCL, a 10 kOhm contrast trimmer on V0. The LCD model draws no backlight current, so the module's white backlight LED is wired across A and K as its own part.",
